LumiAH
======

Moved from LumiRPEngine (https://github.com/TheLiquorPriest/LumiRPEngine), by the same author:

  - The agent loop, the provider session, usage, sessions, compaction and blobs
    (LumiRPEngine src/backend/agents) -> LumiAH src/core.
  - The lexical search index, the tool that reads an earlier turn's work, the receipt a turn leaves
    for the next, and the memo a compaction writes (LumiRPEngine src/engine/lexical.ts and
    src/backend/agents) -> LumiAH src/core.
  - The loopback relay, its stream writer, the link to the extension and the command line that
    installs and runs them (LumiRPEngine src/cli, src/shared/loopback.ts, src/backend/loopback)
    -> LumiAH src/runtime, src/link and src/extension/backend.
  - The drawer's store, scrolling, chat-head measuring, design tokens, component styles and icons,
    and the preview harness (LumiRPEngine src/frontend, dev) -> LumiAH src/extension/frontend,
    dev/preview.

Design taken from LumiAgent by AMousePad (https://github.com/AMousePad/LumiAgent, MIT):

  - The ideas of an agent loop over the host's generation call: tool calls run and their results
    fed back until the model answers, tool calls a model writes as text recovered, large tool
    results clipped with the rest readable from scratch, a detector for repeated identical calls,
    and request and token throttles.

Design taken from Warp by japolino (https://github.com/japolino/warp), with no Warp code retained:

  - The pattern of a per-swipe turn record kept in message metadata, with a path hash chained over
    the messages before it so a record knows whether it is on the current path. LumiAH's anchors
    follow it by way of LumiRPEngine's ledger.

Design taken from Warp Studio by japolino (https://github.com/japolino/warp-studio), with no Warp
Studio code retained:

  - The pattern of one pure core shared by a command line and a server, with only the entry
    touching the file system, by way of LumiRPEngine's command line.


Third-party code in the built bundles
-------------------------------------

dist/lumiah.js, the runtime, contains pi-ai (@earendil-works/pi-ai, MIT) and the packages it
brings along: among them the Anthropic SDK (MIT), the OpenAI SDK (Apache-2.0), and Google's Gen AI
SDK and auth libraries (Apache-2.0). dist/frontend.js contains Preact (MIT). dist/backend.js
contains no third-party code. Each package, its version, copyright notice and licence text are in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
